2. BerryEsseen

addons/berryesseen/BeList.lean and addons/berryesseen/BeObs.lean restate parts of the cover
parser of CoolRmal/BerryEsseen (commit bfb22608ad18) in order to prove the package's own
functions equal to list-based versions, and they share a few pattern-match lines with that
source.

The parse-once add-on in addons/berryesseen_parse_once/ builds on BeList.lean. Its BoCore.lean
reads the package's certificate format in metaprogramming code that follows the same parser,
and states lemmas about the package's definitions. Its scripts/leaves.tsv holds counts derived
from the package's cover data, and the generated modules under gen/ refer to the package's
modules and declarations by name. The certificates themselves are not included: the modules
read them from the package when they are built.

The package has no license file.

3. lean-regex

addons/regex/NTRegexCaseFold.lean copies the definitions checkAllPairs, isLtFirst and noChain of
pandaman64/lean-regex (commit 32af6f33d80e, correctness/RegexCorrectness/Unicode/CaseFold/Data.lean), so
that the kernel can check them equal to the package's own private definitions. lean-regex is under the
Apache License 2.0.

4. longfellow-zk

addons/longfellow/NTLfzk.lean restates some of the certificate functions of longfellow-zk/longfellow-zk
(commit de5f9490c3d8; formal/ligero/CodingTheory/ListDecoding/HahnDelsarte.lean and HahnDelsarteTable.lean,
formal/ligero/examples/Ligero/Certificate.lean) with a fast binomial coefficient, in order to prove the
package's own functions equal to them, and shares a few lines with those files. longfellow-zk is under the
Apache License 2.0 (Copyright © 2025 Google LLC).

